    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0743" n="653" xml:id="pg653"/>

                <head>No. 282.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Sir Edward Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 11,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to our conversation of to-day, in
                    reference to the proposed treaty for reciprocal trade between the United States
                    and the Dominion of Canada, which was submitted to the consideration of the
                    Senate of the United States at the last session of Congress, I have the honor to
                    inform you that the Senate, upon the 3d instant, resolved that it was not deemed
                    expedient to recommend the negotiation of the treaty.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
